{
 "measured": "2026-10-11, production build (next build, next start on localhost:3300), headless Chrome over the DevTools protocol. Not Lighthouse, not a real device, not Safari.",
 "method": {
  "lcp": "PerformanceObserver largest-contentful-paint, median of 3 fresh loads with the cache disabled",
  "layoutShift": "sum of every layout-shift entry without recent input (an upper bound for CLS), at load and after a real scroll to the foot of the page",
  "fontsAndImages": "Resource Timing entries at load",
  "throttling": "slow 4G: 150 ms latency, 1.6 Mbps down, 750 kbps up, 4x CPU"
 },
 "caveats": [
  "Every picture is a drawn stand-in of about 4 KB. LCP with stand-ins says little about LCP with photographs.",
  "At 1440px Chrome does not count the stand-in hero as an LCP candidate (too few bytes for its area), so the element reported there is the h1.",
  "photographWeightHero replaces the hero with a synthetic 188 KB JPEG served through the throttled network. It is a sensitivity test, not a measurement of real VNest photography."
 ],
